IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-cpc-interface`
IMPORT `ea-types`

-- Evidence Act 1893, Part 4 "Bankers' books" (sections 170 to 176), Part 5 (section 177) and the
-- First and Second Schedules.
-- Source: source/EA1893.txt lines 4546 to 4738.
--
-- The questions this module answers: HOW IS AN ENTRY IN A BANKER'S BOOK PROVED (Part 4), IS AN OFFENCE A "CHILD
-- ABUSE OFFENCE" OR A "SEXUAL OFFENCE" (First Schedule, which section 3(1) and sections 124, 154A and the Criminal
-- Procedure Code's sections 264A, 281, 281A and 281B depend on), and IS A BODY A "SPECIFIED STATUTORY BODY" (Second
-- Schedule, which section 80A depends on).
--
-- The Schedules are encoded as printed in the 1 Oct 2026 text.  Section 177 lets the Minister amend them by order in the
-- Gazette; an order made after that date is not reflected: see NOTES.md.

§ `170 to 176. Bankers' books`

-- 170: "bank" and "banker" mean any company carrying on the business of bankers in Singapore under a licence granted under
-- any law relating to banking; "court" in this Part is the General Division of the High Court; "legal proceeding" means any civil or
-- criminal proceeding or inquiry in which evidence is or may be given, and includes an arbitration.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 170 'bank' and 'banker'"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankers Books Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is a bank` IF
    b's `the company carries on the business of bankers in Singapore under a licence granted under a law relating to banking`

-- 172(1): a copy of an entry in a banker's book is not to be received in evidence under the Part unless it is first proved that (a)
-- the book was at the time of the entry one of the ordinary books of the bank; (b) the entry was made in the usual and ordinary course
-- of business; and (c) the book is in the custody or control of the bank.  172(2): the proof may be given by an officer of the bank,
-- orally or by affidavit.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 172(1)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankers Books Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the book is proved to be a banker's book under section 172` IF
        b's `the book was, at the time of the making of the entry, one of the ordinary books of the bank`
    AND b's `the entry was made in the usual and ordinary course of business`
    AND b's `the book is in the custody or control of the bank`

-- 173(1): a copy is not to be received unless it is further proved that the copy has been examined with the original entry and is
-- correct.  173(2): proof by a person who has examined the copy with the original entry, orally or by affidavit.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 173(1)"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankers Books Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the copy is proved to be a verified copy under section 173` IF
    b's `the copy has been examined with the original entry and is correct`

-- 171: subject to the Part, a copy of any entry in a banker's book is in all legal proceedings to be received as prima facie evidence of
-- the entry and of the matters, transactions and accounts recorded.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, ss 171, 172 and 173"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankers Books Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the copy of the entry is received as prima facie evidence of the entry and of the matters recorded` IF
        `the book is proved to be a banker's book under section 172` b
    AND `the copy is proved to be a verified copy under section 173` b
    AND `the company is a bank` b

-- 174: an officer of a bank is not, in any legal proceedings to which the bank is not a party, compellable to produce any banker's book the
-- contents of which can be proved under the Part, or to appear as a witness to prove the matters recorded, unless by order of a judge made
-- for special cause.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 174"
GIVEN b IS A `Bankers Books Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer of the bank is compellable to produce the book or appear under section 174` IF
        b's `the bank is a party to the legal proceeding`
    OR  b's `a judge has ordered the production or attendance for special cause`

-- 175: on the application of any party to a legal proceeding the court or a Judge may order that the party be at liberty to inspect and take
-- copies of entries in a banker's book (a discretion); 176: costs.  Both are inert here.

§ `First Schedule. Child abuse offences and sexual offences`

-- First Schedule, Part 1 "Child abuse offences": 1. any offence under section 6(1), 7, 8, 14(2), 16 or 17 of the Children and Young Persons
-- Act 1993; 2. any offence under section 377BG, 377BH, 377BI, 377BJ, 377BK or 377BL of the Penal Code 1871.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, First Schedule, Part 1, items 1 and 2"
`the sections of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993 that create child abuse offences` MEANS
    LIST "6(1)", "7", "8", "14(2)", "16", "17"

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, First Schedule, Part 1, item 2"
`the sections of the Penal Code 1871 that create child abuse offences` MEANS
    LIST "377BG", "377BH", "377BI", "377BJ", "377BK", "377BL"

-- First Schedule, Part 2 "Sexual offences": 1. any offence under section 354, 354A, 355, 372, 373, 373A, 375, 376, 376A, 376AA, 376B, 376C,
-- 376D, 376E, 376EA, 376EB, 376EC, 376ED, 376EE, 376F, 376G, 376H, 377(3), 377B(3), 377BA, 377BB, 377BC, 377BD, 377BE or 377BF of the
-- Penal Code 1871; 2. any offence under section 140, 141, 142, 143, 144, 145, 146, 146A, 147 or 148 of the Women's Charter 1961.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, First Schedule, Part 2, item 1"
`the sections of the Penal Code 1871 that create sexual offences` MEANS
    LIST "354", "354A", "355", "372", "373", "373A", "375", "376", "376A", "376AA", "376B", "376C", "376D", "376E", "376EA", "376EB", "376EC", "376ED", "376EE", "376F", "376G", "376H", "377(3)", "377B(3)", "377BA", "377BB", "377BC", "377BD", "377BE", "377BF"

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, First Schedule, Part 2, item 2"
`the sections of the Women's Charter 1961 that create sexual offences` MEANS
    LIST "140", "141", "142", "143", "144", "145", "146", "146A", "147", "148"

-- Section 3(1): "child abuse offence" and "sexual offence" each include attempting to commit, abetting the commission of, or being a party to a
-- criminal conspiracy to commit, such an offence.  The class of an ancillary offence is the class of the offence it is ancillary to.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 3(1) 'child abuse offence' and 'sexual offence'; First Schedule"
GIVEN o IS A `Scheduled Offence Facts`
GIVETH A `Kind of Offence Class`
`the class of the offence under the First Schedule` MEANS
    BRANCH IF     o's `the Act under which the offence is created` EQUALS "Children and Young Persons Act 1993"
              AND elem (o's `the section number`) `the sections of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993 that create child abuse offences`
           THEN `a child abuse offence`
           IF     o's `the Act under which the offence is created` EQUALS "Penal Code 1871"
              AND elem (o's `the section number`) `the sections of the Penal Code 1871 that create child abuse offences`
           THEN `a child abuse offence`
           IF     o's `the Act under which the offence is created` EQUALS "Penal Code 1871"
              AND elem (o's `the section number`) `the sections of the Penal Code 1871 that create sexual offences`
           THEN `a sexual offence`
           IF     o's `the Act under which the offence is created` EQUALS "Women's Charter 1961"
              AND elem (o's `the section number`) `the sections of the Women's Charter 1961 that create sexual offences`
           THEN `a sexual offence`
           OTHERWISE `neither`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 3(1) 'child abuse offence'"
GIVEN o IS A `Scheduled Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a child abuse offence under section 3(1)` IF
    `the class of the offence under the First Schedule` o EQUALS `a child abuse offence`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 3(1) 'sexual offence'"
GIVEN o IS A `Scheduled Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a sexual offence under section 3(1)` IF
    `the class of the offence under the First Schedule` o EQUALS `a sexual offence`

§ `Second Schedule. Specified statutory bodies`

-- Second Schedule: the twenty-three statutory bodies, and the Act under which each is established, whose films are within section 80A.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, Second Schedule, items 1 to 23"
`the specified statutory bodies` MEANS
    LIST
        (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Building and Construction Authority", "Building and Construction Authority Act 1999")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Central Provident Fund Board", "Central Provident Fund Act 1953")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore", "Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore Act 2009")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Civil Service College", "Civil Service College Act 2001")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Defence Science and Technology Agency", "Defence Science and Technology Agency Act 2000")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Enterprise Singapore Board", "Enterprise Singapore Board Act 2018")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Economic Development Board", "Economic Development Board Act 1961")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Health Sciences Authority", "Health Sciences Authority Act 2001")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Home Team Science and Technology Agency", "Home Team Science and Technology Agency Act 2019")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Housing and Development Board", "Housing and Development Act 1959")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Info-communications Media Development Authority", "Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore", "Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore Act 1992")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Intellectual Property Office of Singapore", "Intellectual Property Office of Singapore Act 2001")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Jurong Town Corporation", "Jurong Town Corporation Act 1968")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Land Transport Authority of Singapore", "Land Transport Authority of Singapore Act 1995")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore", "Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore Act 1996")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Monetary Authority of Singapore", "Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "National Parks Board", "National Parks Board Act 1996")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Public Utilities Board", "Public Utilities Act 2001")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Singapore Food Agency", "Singapore Food Agency Act 2019")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Singapore Land Authority", "Singapore Land Authority Act 2001")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Singapore Tourism Board", "Singapore Tourism Board Act 1963")
      , (`Statutory Body Row` OF "Urban Redevelopment Authority", "Urban Redevelopment Authority Act 1989")

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 80A(5) 'specified statutory body'; Second Schedule"
GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a specified statutory body in the Second Schedule` IF
    any (`has the name`) `the specified statutory bodies`
    WHERE
        `has the name` row MEANS row's `statutory body` EQUALS name

-- 177: the Minister may by order in the Gazette amend the First and Second Schedules.  Orders are not encoded.
